From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 07:47:50 -0400
Subject: spread the Space switcher across the sidebar

The chips were crammed into the bottom-left corner at 24 DIP with a reserved
name row above them, which read as broken -- the operator's words -- next to
the reference, whose icons spread evenly across the sidebar's width.

The row is now chips at 28 DIP with a flexible spacer after each, so they
distribute across the full width with the new-Space button at the trailing end.
The reserved name row is gone; the name lives in the tooltip. Renaming still
happens in place: the icon row swaps for a field of the same height.

Hit-testing and the context menu go through an explicit chip list rather than
child indices, because the spacers made index arithmetic wrong.

Why: operator feedback on the first DMG.
Removable when: never, short of dropping Spaces.
